# Trivy ignore policy.
#
# Keep this file empty unless a finding is accepted deliberately. Use a
# reviewed OpenVEX statement for package-applicability decisions.
#
# jq is the only exception authority: the gate scan does not pass this file
# to trivy. scripts/ci/security/lint-trivyignore.sh validates every entry
# and fails on malformed, expired or over-aged lines.
#
# Each entry accepts one Ubuntu OS finding, scoped to a package and a target:
#
# CVE-YYYY-NNNN #reason:<text>;pkg:<name>;target:<target>;review:<ticket>;exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# - review ticket: #<number> or <PROJECT>-<number> (a reviewed decision)
# - exp: a real calendar date, strictly after today and at most 90 days ahead
# - no whitespace after the field colons; fields appear in this fixed order
# - only HIGH affected / CRITICAL will_not_fix Ubuntu findings can use an
#   exception; see docs/decisions/0011-image-vulnerability-gate.md
#
# Expired entries must be removed or renewed with a fresh review decision.
